      },
      "text": "The Argentine Side of Iguazú Falls"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b9ad3e14216c2f08",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "77e9684690633f7f4cd620a4de3e80c7647e1754ff9d3ef1e359ac84ee06fbe1",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-translator-20261110-da7adf1e0510432f",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, we cross the Tancredo Neves Bridge over the Iguazú River for a tour of the Argentine side.\n\nThe trails here let you see the falls from different heights and distances. You’ll walk beside cascades and reach viewpoints with a clear view of the Devil’s Throat. Over the course of the day, you’ll see the falls from above and below, get close to the falling water and spend time in the park surrounding the falls. Along some walkways, the water runs almost level with the decking, so you can pick out individual cascades amid the overall roar. Visiting both sides of Iguazú gives you a wide view of the whole waterfall system as well as a close look at its individual cascades."
    },
